WEBVTT

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.870
Calm down, Poppy.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.820
<i>How are you, Mum? It's me, Alice.</i>

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.320
<i>I'm in second grade now in high school.</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.790
Wake up. It's morning.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.940
Shino, good morning.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.320
Good morning, Alice.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.030
<i>Shino's still not a morning riser.</i>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.080
<i>She always needs my help to get up.</i>

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.670
Shinobu! Alice-chan! Time for school!

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.090
Alice.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:11.850
Huh?

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.810
Good morning.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.600
Isami, good morning.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.310
Morning.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.250
<i>Isami is in university now.</i>

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.980
Oh my, Alice...

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.640
Your blonde hair's looking duller this year.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.490
What?

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.200
That's a lie! A lie!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.700
It's not true!

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.370
Alice's hair is shinier than ever!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.330
I'm joking.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.500
Onee-chan...

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.750
There are certain things you shouldn't joke about!

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.260
You always get your kicks
scaring me like that, Onee-chan!

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.760
Morning!

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:52.800
Hey.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:53.960
Morning.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.870
Good morning.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.640
Shino, what's wrong?

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.630
My older sister was mean to me this morning...

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.250
Isa-nee hasn't changed a bit.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:08.100
<i>My friends Aya and Youko are doing well, too.</i>

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.340
Good mornin'!

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.100
Oh, Karen! Good morning.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.200
Your blonde hair looks wonderful today.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.350
Morning!

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.280
Morning.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.730
You, too, Alice!

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.960
<i>Oh my God, Karen's full of energy as always.</i>

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.960
Quit messing around. Let's go inside.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.220
<i> A new school year has begun,
so my classroom has changed.</i>

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.410
<i>Shino and I aren't classmates anymore.</i>

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.720
Good mornin'!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.820
Karen-chan.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:46.920
Morning.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.090
Morning, Karen-chan.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.970
Good mornin'!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.790
Good mornin'!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.370
I should go, too.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.640
Okay...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.760
I'll see you during break, Alice.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.120
Okay!

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.270
Alice, let's go.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.230
Okay!

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.680
<i>This is my second spring in Japan.</i>

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.210
<i>I'm really looking forward to having
fun with Shino and my friends!</i>

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.440
I miss Shino...

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.030
That was quick! We haven't
even had morning assembly yet!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.680
Ayaya!

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.350
Spring Is Here

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.350
What? Where'd that come from?

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.600
Duckface! It's totally in right now!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.590
There were a few things wrong with that.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.110
I don't think it's all that popular now, either.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.950
Karen-chan! Here, have some sweets.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.100
Oh, Honoka!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.420
Thank you!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.660
Sorry Karen never gives anything to you.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:56.750
It's okay.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.530
You were very nice to me last year, too!

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.870
Don't take gifts for granted.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.770
You should give her something in return.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.660
Y-You don't have to worry about that...

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.150
Oh, you're right!

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:07.890
Smooch!

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.050
Hey!

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.640
Stand.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.270
Bow.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.610
Good morning.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.770
Sit.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.380
Attendance Book

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.860
Good morning, everyone.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:35.120
Let's begin homeroom.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.490
Your hair's so pretty, Alice.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.010
It looks so fluffy.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.550
Hey, Alice.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.790
Can you help me with this?

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.310
Sure.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.040
Talk to you later.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.130
Okay, later.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.340
I'm having fun making friends
with my new classmates.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.200
Really? That's good.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.800
But Shino's not here...

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.810
Oh, come on. Get used to it already.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.110
You've got this one wrong.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.690
What should it be?

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.200
Youko...

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.050
Do you know all of your times tables?

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.450
Alice, you're making fun of me, aren't you?

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.700
Okay, let's get morning homeroom started.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.480
With the same homeroom teacher,
it doesn't feel like we've moved up a grade.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.250
Really? I'm glad Karasuma-sensei
is our homeroom teacher.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.860
<i>I wonder what Alice is doing right now...</i>

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.470
<i>I know!</i>

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.620
<i>Alice... Alice...</i>

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.490
<i>Can you hear my voice?</i>

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.340
<i>Alice...</i>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:45.230
<i>Shino's in real trouble!</i>

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.480
I think I just heard Shino's voice...

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:50.890
Seriously?

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.860
Yeah. I'm sure it was her.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.740
Really? What did she say?

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.950
She said we're having gratin for dinner tonight.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.180
You meant Shino's mom?

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.640
<i>Neither of them are diligent students,</i>

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.910
<i>so I'll have to keep an eye on them.</i>

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.720
Nice!

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.920
This isn't bad, either.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.610
Kujou-san, read the next one.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.480
Y-Yes, sir! U-Um...

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.610
Aya-chan, can I use the telephone
game to tell her the answer?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.450
The telephone game?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:32.980
Yes.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.290
Um, I mean...

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.330
Teacher!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:40.890
Yes?

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.930
Can Oomiya-san and I switch seats?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.020
Aya-chan?

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.040
Why?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.970
You couldn't get any studying done here.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.710
You might not advance to the next grade.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.260
What?

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:00.050
Don't blame me if you get a
negative score on your next test.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:02.390
A negative score? That's possible?!

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.480
<i>Now, finally...</i>

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.100
<i>For some reason, this hour feels really long.</i>

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.150
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:16.110
<i>this is my first class without Youko.</i>

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:19.050
<i>Why do I keep thinking about Youko?</i>

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:20.860
<i>We're not in a long-distance relationship...</i>

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:21.640
<i>Aya...</i>

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:22.910
<i>Aya...</i>

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.720
I just came to see Alice!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.680
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:35.960
About what?

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:41.420
I was thinking about you
all through class, Shino.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:44.470
I think about you even more when we're apart.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:48.350
I bet our hearts are perfectly in sync now.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.850
Then what do you want to eat right now?

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.670
Um...

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.670
Dumplings with sweet sauce!

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.670
Shrimp doria!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.600
I messed up.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:00.300
I was going to say shrimp doria with
a side of dumplings with sweet sauce.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:01.490
Boom

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.530
We were thinking the same thing.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:02.880
They forced it.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:03.760
That sounds disgusting.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.890
And when I introduced myself in my new class,

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.000
I told everyone about you.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.880
Shino is a wonderful person!

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.860
You're embarrassing me.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.070
We did introductions in our class, too.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:22.180
Oh, yeah. Karen kept going
on and on, even when

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.310
we all tried to get her to stop. And...

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.570
I'm sorry.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.020
Karen?

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.270
I met a tiger.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.100
Roar

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.320
A tiger?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.210
Our homeroom teacher,
Kuzehashi-sensei, got mad at her.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:37.520
That's the home ec teacher, isn't it?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.900
I'm jealous that Class C's homeroom
teacher is Karasuma-sensei!

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.040
I like how serious Kuzehashi-sensei is...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.280
She's scary!

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.990
If she were an animal, she'd be a tiger!

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:52.510
She's probably already eaten a few students!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.650
Karen...

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.880
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.210
Kujou-san.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.420
You're the only one who hasn't
turned in their handout.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.650
Also, you fall asleep too much!

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:06.240
And wear your uniform properly! You're too gaudy!

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.180
Tie your long hair up, too!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.470
B-But it looks cute, doesn't it?

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.640
<i>She's going to eat me!</i>

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.480
Um, I'm sorry. Karen doesn't mean any harm.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.280
No, she's 100% in the wrong.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.070
Now, now...

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.880
<i>Youko's so bold.</i>

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.970
<i>Because she's a bear?</i>

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.990
<i>Which is stronger, a bear or a tiger?</i>

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.250
I know! I bet a grizzly would beat a tiger!

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:35.120
What are you talking about?!
This is <i>your</i> problem!

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.000
Be more careful with your
uniform and your attitude.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.030
Turn in your handout by the end of the day.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.060
Understood?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.970
She seems nice.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:49.940
What?

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.180
She gave you advice.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.250
What?

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.020
What?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.650
She's scary when she's angry.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.700
Actually, I forgot something

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.420
for home ec this afternoon...

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.340
Karen.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:09.150
People forget things all the time.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:12.950
I'm sure Kuzehashi-sensei will be
understanding if you talk to her.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.360
Shino...

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.110
Either way, you'll still probably get in trouble.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.300
I have an idea!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.700
I'll follow the teacher
around and get dirt on her,

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.200
so she can't get mad at me.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.100
That's it!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.110
Don't you have other things to do?!

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.460
Don't run in the hallway!

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.640
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.530
Target acquired.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.650
Let's not follow her, you guys...

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:43.820
She's leaving.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.320
How can we get dirt on her?

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.030
Good question...

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.590
Do you need something?

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:07.150
N-N-N-No, nothing! Nothing at all!

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:08.430
That's fine, then.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:09.620
But Oomiya-san...

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.370
Yes, ma'am?

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.390
You're on class duty today, right?

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.270
Tell everyone to gather
their assignments together

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.820
before the closing assembly.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.640
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:20.880
U-Um...

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.230
I'll do it, even if it costs me my life!

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:25.420
Here I go!

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.980
Shino, that's the way to the gym, not Class A!

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.970
Wait for me!

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.740
<i>I was only looking at her...</i>

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:40.960
<i>No... No one likes being stared at.</i>

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:45.280
<i>But my students are so cute,
I can't help but stare...</i>

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:54.220
Don't move.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.110
You have something on your eyelid.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.750
Okay, you're all good now.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.620
Thanks, Sensei.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.560
<i>She was only looking, too,
so why is the reaction so different?</i>

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:05.190
Faculty Office

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:07.980
Kuzehashi-sensei, you always
look so cool in your suits.

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.680
A teacher must serve as an
example to her students.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:13.560
I mustn't dress sloppily.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.950
Yes, you're right.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.050
Tracksuits aren't really...

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.790
Oh, no, I think you're fine the way you are.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.880
Um, Sensei...

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:26.880
Do you have any suggestions on
how to make my students like me?

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:27.780
What?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.190
I always seem to scare my students.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:33.070
What should I do?

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.550
Well...

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.330
Rabbit ears.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:40.280
If you wear those, your class will love you.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.890
They're so cute! You should try it.

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:46.190
No, no. Those really aren't my style...

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.440
Rabbit ears aside,

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.640
you'll be fine if you just smile.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:04.170
No, this just isn't me.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.830
I give up.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:12.090
Shino, what do you think of Kuzehashi-sensei?

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.550
I fall asleep a lot, too,
so I worry she'll get mad at me.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.720
But I think she's a little like my sister.

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:22.890
Like Isa-nee?

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.430
I know what you mean.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:25.440
It's her eyes.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.330
She may scold or tease you,

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.900
but her eyes are full of love deep inside.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.650
Welcome back.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.000
I'm back.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:35.840
Welcome back.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.340
Welcome back.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:37.520
How'd it go?

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:39.910
I see.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:40.660
But...

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.380
I think Kuzehashi-sensei and I will become friends.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:48.750
She reminds me of me when I came to Japan.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.670
How I couldn't make any friends...

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.680
She must've been trying to stretch
out her forehead wrinkles!

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:58.180
K-Karen...

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:04.060
Kujou-san!

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.120
You forgot something <i>again?</i>

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.220
How many times must I tell you—

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.710
<i>It should be okay!</i>

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:12.320
<i>She's a tiger with kind eyes!</i>

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.190
Don't worry! I won't forget next time!

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:20.640
You don't seem very apologetic, Kujou-san.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.500
The tiger was just a tiger, after all...

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:30.950
<i>Oomiya Shinobu.</i>

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.230
<i>Home country: Japan.</i>

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.140
<i>Personality: kind.</i>

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:38.570
<i>She loves foreign countries and
wants to be an interpreter.</i>

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:42.460
<i>She's difficult to understand
and a little mysterious.</i>

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.090
Nice and cool...

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.320
What are you doing?

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.600
Don't look!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.570
Are you investigating Shino?

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.190
Number one!

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.340
Two!

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:02.610
You guys, too!

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.910
Huh? Three!

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:04.910
Four!

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.360
Why are we sounding off?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:10.020
We're members of the Shino Fan Club!

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:11.700
I never joined that!

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.000
What do you want to know about Shino?

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.710
I want to know everything about her.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:21.040
We're all good friends of hers,

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.710
but we still have trouble
understanding what Shino is thinking.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.910
I guess that's true...

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.260
She's always smiling, but maybe secretly...

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.830
I'm sorry for deceiving you.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.470
I'm actually...

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:41.390
a member of an evil organization!

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:42.480
So cool!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.680
That sounds interesting.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.780
I'll help.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:46.680
Me, too.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.820
Then let the top secret
Shino investigation begin!

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:51.630
Yeah!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.250
Hello, Shino. How are you?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:01.010
Oh, yes. I'm happy-happy.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.500
Shino, I know you like foreign countries,

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.760
but what else do you like?

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.100
Well...

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.820
I like you, Alice.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:13.260
Oh, stop!

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:16.280
Not that! I'm glad to hear it, though!

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:18.170
No good! Next!

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.500
Shino, do you have a second?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.390
Yes?

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.460
You look worried.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.840
You can tell me what's wrong, if you want.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.900
Really?

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:32.990
Come to think of it, Aya-chan,
is something worrying you?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:33.570
Huh?

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:37.390
You've seemed down since we changed classes.

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.120
You can tell me what's wrong, if you'd like.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:43.580
It's true! Will you listen to my problems?

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.210
Hey!

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.460
Unbelievable.

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.210
You're all so helpless.

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:51.010
Let Detective Karen handle this!

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:53.790
Shino!

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.560
I bet your favorite pattern is...

00:16:57.560 --> 00:16:58.850
polka dots!

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.080
I like polka dots.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.770
Do you like the Union Jack?

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:04.150
What?

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:06.440
How did you know?

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.040
Everyone knows that.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.660
Our investigation has revealed the following:

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.030
Favorite pattern: polka dots.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:21.660
Dislikes insects, if anything. Also, barking dogs.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.160
That's all we've learned?

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.670
We need some more personal information.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.090
Maybe there are some hints
hidden in Shino's childhood.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:31.620
That makes sense.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.370
Actually, a long time ago...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.220
Let's guess what the other is thinking.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:41.190
Okay.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:42.890
Let's see...

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.910
"I'm hungry!"

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.660
Nope.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.080
I was thinking about

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.010
world peace.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:51.650
Huh?

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.440
It's no use.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.120
I just can't understand her.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.050
Sorry.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.700
Don't give up, Youko!

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.260
Try to remember!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.910
There must be something!

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:05.220
Looks like there's nothing we can do.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.120
What a letdown.

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.590
Looks like it's an unsolved mystery.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.050
No!

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:12.670
I want to know more about Shino!

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:13.930
Alice...

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.930
I want to share her joy,

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.430
and help her when she's in trouble!

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:21.590
I want to become her true friend!

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:22.600
You're that serious?

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.990
Alice, the other day, were you worrying

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:29.090
about the other blonde friend

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:32.420
she may have had before she met you?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.860
No! That's got nothing to do with this!

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:36.160
Come on, Karen!

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:38.140
This is sounding like an
investigation into an affair.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.240
What made you think that?

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.410
Well, you know Shino likes blonde hair.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.100
Blonde Girls Club

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.340
How wonderful.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.680
When I thought about it,

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.530
Blondes are the best!

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:55.300
the first time I met Shino in England...

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.680
She's blonde! She's a blonde girl!

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:03.280
She already loved blonde hair.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.310
Shino loves foreign countries

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:08.190
more than blonde hair.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.070
Though, she loves blonde, too.

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.400
Why did Shino fall in love
with foreign countries?

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.520
I think it all started with her homestay.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.630
Before that...

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:25.030
Well, I thought the Union Jack looked cute.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.100
Thanks for waiting for me. Let's go home.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.920
You were all acting so secretive today.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:39.960
I wish you'd asked me to join you.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:41.400
Sorry, Shino!

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:42.680
It was a secret investigation.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:46.680
You did a homestay just because you
thought the Union Jack was cute?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.930
Mostly. But also because,
when I was in grade school,

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:53.190
I met an old foreign lady at the
train station who needed help.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.850
Excuse me, young lady.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:59.270
Do you know which bus goes to the hospital?

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:01.970
But I couldn't understand her.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.470
What's the matter? Can I help you?

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.480
I'd like to go to the general hospital.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.300
Oh, you may want to take
the bus, number three,

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:13.840
from the south exit of the station terminal.

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:15.280
When she was in trouble,

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:18.590
a lady fluent in English saved her.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.190
Since then, I've wanted to bring people

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:23.940
together through the power of words.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.830
That sounds just like you.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:28.350
Huh?

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:31.520
So that's why you wanted
to become an interpreter,

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.790
and why you came to my
house for a homestay.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.800
That's great, Alice!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:36.360
Yeah!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.440
Sorry I doubted you.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:41.740
Your heart and mind are as open as the sky.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:45.340
It purifies my own tarnished heart.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:48.520
I can feel the negative ions!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:50.370
The air is so fresh!

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.870
What's gotten into you two?

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:55.810
We learned a little more about Shino.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:59.460
Yeah. She's very straightforward
about what she likes.

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.380
She has no ulterior motives.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.390
Shino, want to wear my jacket?

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.260
Really, Karen?

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.250
I warmed it up for you.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.230
Karen!

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:17.650
Try and catch me!

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.960
Wait up!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.750
Aya, let's go!

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:22.770
Huh?

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:24.830
Hey, wait up!

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:24.830
Jeez...

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:28.300
Wait for me!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.700
You can't catch me!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:36.030
<i>But what really made me decide
to become an interpreter</i>

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:39.420
<i>was that homestay when I met Alice.</i>

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.420
Shino?

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:43.560
What?

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.930
Nothing.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:47.210
How's that?

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:49.670
No! Stop it!

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:52.780
Youko, you're going too far.

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:23.100
I'm sad we're not classmates anymore.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.750
But we're always together before
and after school, and during breaks.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:28.240
You're right! To bring us closer,

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.470
let's walk home on three legs!

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.470
Oh, good idea!

00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:30.070
Good Idea!

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:31.680
What happened?!

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.160
Tripped

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:33.160
Ragged

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.340
It was a bad idea...

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:35.500
Present For You

00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:34.500
See you...

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:35.500
Hang in there!
